      ],
      "context_before_ids": [],
      "context_after_ids": [],
      "context_text": "Okay everyone, like we can begin. just to to clarify, this is a introductory course at California State University Bakersfield on the religions of Asia. And this week in particular, we are taking a look at the Jane tradition and we are fortunate to have with us some guest speakers to teach us more about the tradition from their perspective. These are people who have practiced the religion for quite some time and can share with us. some basics on Jane ideas, philosophy and practice. And hopefully we'll have some chance at the end for questions as well. So I want to begin with a greeting which I learned from my Jain friends over the last couple of years, Jai Jin Indra, which is, Shaileshya Didi maybe the best way to explain that, you can correct me if I'm wrong, but it's something like homage to the victor, the Jina.",
      "start_timestamp": null,
      "end_timestamp": null,
      "boundary_reason": "max_sentences",
      "forced_boundary": false,
      "oversize": false
    },
